=== F-1 FIX ADDENDUM (Phase 3 impl review, iteration 1 — BLOCKING finding) ===
Executed 2026-07-09, same worktree.

Finding: promote_gate_run.py:239-241 passed assessment["combined_score"] (unitless Sharpe-like
ratio) as compute_realized_gate's mean_backtest_net_usd (REQ-RL11's DOLLAR-scale per-trade mean),
so data_realism_gap compared a ratio against real dollar figures — wrong-unit, blocking/deadlocking
promotion decorative-ly. Fix: pass assessment["mean_oos_net_usd"] instead, and make
compute_realized_gate None-safe (mean_oos_net_usd is None for scope-guard-rejected/stage1-failed
candidates, computed unconditionally before the eligibility check).

Files changed:
  lib/promote_gate.py — compute_realized_gate(mean_backtest_net_usd: Optional[float], ...):
    docstring extended with the None semantics; realism_gap_blocks now short-circuits to False
    when mean_backtest_net_usd is None (skips gate_math.data_realism_gap entirely — the
    fixture-vs-reality contradiction is undefined without a fixture claim, not trivially true or
    false) instead of calling float(None). REQ-RL13a's 13-key schema is unchanged.
  lib/promote_gate_run.py:239-244 — compute_realized_gate's mean_backtest_net_usd= now reads
    assessment["mean_oos_net_usd"] (was assessment["combined_score"]).
  tests/test_wiring.py — 3 new regression tests (below).

